00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:04.000
So this is big O notation, capital O notation.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.000
So we have f of n equals big O of g of n.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:17.000
This means that there are some suitable constants,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:34.080
c and n not, such that f is bounded by c times g of n

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.880
for all sufficiently large n.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.480
So this is a pretty intuitive notion.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.360
We've seen it before.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.380
We're going to assume that f of n is non-negative here.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:50.060
And I just want f of n to be bounded above by g of n.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:56.340
So we've seen a bunch of examples, but something like 2

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.280
times n squared is big o of n cubed.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.540
Define.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.000
And roughly this means if you drop leading constants and

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:09.000
lower order terms then this is less than or equal to that.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
So big O corresponds roughly to less than or equal to.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.000
But this is the formalization. Another way to think of it

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.000
formally as -- so a funny thing about this notation is this

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.000
asymmetric. Normally you think of a

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.000
quality being symmetric. A equals B then B equals a. But it's not true here.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:31.000
We don't have n cubed being big O of n squared.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
You don't even have big O of n cubed equal to n squared.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.000
So we'll see exactly what that means in a second.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:49.000
But before we get there, so this is a bit bizarre notation, and you should always think about what it really means.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Another way to think about what it really means is that f(n) is in some set of functions

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:13.640
that are like g. So you could define big o of g(n) to be a set of functions. Let's call it f of n such that there exists constants.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.800
You have the same definition.

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.320
I think fancy here.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:27.000
C and n naught, such that we have the bound f of n is between 0 and c times

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.000
g of n.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:35.000
OK, so a bit of a long definition.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
That's why we use the notation to avoid having to write this

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
over and over. So, you can think of,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.240
instead of n squared being equal to big o of n cubed, what we really mean is that 2n squared is

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:50.440
in the set big o of n cubed.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:56.320
So when we write equal sign, we in some sense mean this

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.800
in the set.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.400
But we're going to use equal sign.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.560
You could write this, and occasionally you see papers

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:06.400
that write this, but this is the notation then that we're going to use.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:07.440
So that has the consequence.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:13.480
The equal sign is asymmetric, just like this operator.

