00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:00.000
if you do some macro programming or something.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:10.000
But it's a bit more mathematical.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.000
So we've defined bigger notation and the equals big O

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.000
of something.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.000
And so we've only defined big O when, on the equal sign,

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:26.000
we have big O of some function. But it's useful to have some general expression on the right

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.000
hand side that involves big O.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.000
So, for example, let's say we have f of n is n cubed plus

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.000
order n squared. So, this is attempting to get an

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.000
error bound. This is saying f n is basically n cubed,

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.000
but there's these lower order terms that are big O of n squared. So this is attempting to get an error bound. This is saying, fn is basically n cubed,

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.000
but there's these lower order terms that are big o of n

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.000
squared.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.000
And so this means that there's a function,

00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:01.000
so I'm short-hand for a function, h of n,

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:11.000
which is in big o of n squared, or equals big o of n squared.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:19.000
Such that f of n equals n cubed plus h of n.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.000
So saying there's some lower order terms that are bounded above by some constant

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.840
times n squared for sufficiently large n.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.680
And that's what's here.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.600
And then f of n equals-- now this is a true equality--

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.840
n cubed plus that error term.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.080
So this is-- you're very useful here.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.840
Essentially, I'm expressing what the lead constant is.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.680
And then saying, well, there's other stuff in it's all

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.200
at most n squared.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.240
Saying that f of n, therefore, is also order n cubed.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:46.000
But that's a bit weaker of a statement.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.000
This is a bit more refined.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:51.000
We want you to use this too often, but it's useful.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Sometimes we'll see, like in last class, we even had a big O

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.000
inside a summation. So you can use them all over the

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.000
place. The point is they represent some

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:03.000
function in that set. A bit less intuitive,

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.000
and this is more subtle,

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:11.000
is what it means to have bigger on the left-hand side.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:16.000
It means the same thing, but there's some convention what

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:22.000
equality means. And this is why equal sign is asymmetric.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.600
Equals means, you should read equals like is.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:32.680
So is means that everything over here is something over here.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.800
So there's an implicit for all on the left-hand side,

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.600
and there exists on the right-hand side.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.000
This is a true statement.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.560
Anything that is n squared plus big o of n

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:44.360
is also big o of n squared, but not the other way around.

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.480
So this is a bit asymmetric.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.400
If you think about it, this is pretty intuitive,

00:08:53.400 --> 00:09:15.000
but it's subtle, so you should be careful. [ Writing on Board ]

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:19.000
So this says for any expansion of the macro on the left-hand side,

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:26.040
which would be f of n, there's an expansion of the macro on the right-hand side,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.320
such that we get equality.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:32.000
And what this allows you to do is

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:35.280
if you have a chain of equal sign relations, a chain of ises,

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.400
then the very first one is equal to or bounded

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.600
by the very last one.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.960
So you can chain equal signs in the way you normally would.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.960
You just can't flip them around.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:45.460
Good. So that's big O notation.
